<!--
    GRTubeYou: the bug report tile icon.

    Why a real Material glyph and not a hand-drawn PNG like the SmartTube settings icons:
    every neighbouring tile is a flat white silhouette filling nearly the whole 302x302 canvas
    (the gear measures 298x298 inside it, search 286x286). A shape drawn by eye does not hold
    that line weight and that fill, and the first attempt at this one came out as an unreadable
    blob - the legs sank into the body. `bug_report` from the same Material set the rest of the
    app already draws from is a verified silhouette at exactly this weight, so it sits among its
    neighbours instead of shouting over them.

    Scale 0.94 leaves a ~3% margin, matching the small inset the neighbours carry. The view box
    stays the Material 24x24 so the path is unmodified.

    White, like the neighbours: settings_card.xml has no tint of its own, so the fill colour is
    what reaches the screen.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="70dp"
    android:height="70dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">

    <group
        android:scaleX="0.94"
        android:scaleY="0.94"
        android:pivotX="12"
        android:pivotY="12">

        <path
            android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
